7. Complete Dynamical System

7.1 State Variables

x_t = (K_{C,t}, K_{R,t}, L_t, w_t, \lambda_t, \mathcal{A}_t, V_t),

where \mathcal{A}_t = (A_E, A_O^\lambda, A_F, A_S, A_C) and V_t is a voice/democracy index (V-Dem electoral democracy, union density, or collective-bargaining coverage). The V_t variable enters the Layer 5 governance feedback; it addresses the political-economy gap that the v0.2 model could not represent.

7.2 Controls

u_t = (g_{R,t}, \tau_t, s_t, \iota_{E,t}),

where g_{R,t} is robotic-capital growth, \tau_t is the tax/transfer rate, s_t is institutional investment, and \iota_{E,t} is energy-efficiency R&D investment.

7.3 Transition Equations

K_{R,t+1} = (1 - \delta_R + g_{R,t})\, K_{R,t},

K_{C,t+1} = (1 - \delta_C)\, K_{C,t} + I_{C,t},

\lambda_{t+1} = \lambda_t + A_{O,t}^\lambda (1-\lambda_t)\, \Delta t,

A_{j,t+1} = A_{j,t}\bigl(1 + g_j(A_{j,t}, s_t)\bigr), \quad j \in \{E, O, F, S, C\},

e_{t+1}(i) = (1 - \delta_e)\, e_t(i) - \iota_{E,t}\, \xi(i),

V_{t+1} = V_t + h_V(RDD_{\text{median},t}, V_t).

The governance-feedback function h_V is deliberately left general. Recent evidence (Lall 2025, APSA preprint) suggests the sign of \partial h_V/\partial RDD_{\text{median}} may be negative in some European contexts: AI-exposed workers are less supportive of redistribution, not more. This sign is not imposed; it is treated as an empirical parameter.

