13. Minimal Testable Prediction

Central prediction.

\frac{\partial \text{RDD}_h}{\partial \theta_h^{\text{eff}}} > 0, \qquad \frac{\partial \text{RDD}_h}{\partial \text{exposure}_h} < 0,

with the first dominating when \lambda is high and the second when \lambda is low.

Empirical implication. Two economies with identical K_R but different \lambda have different RDD distributions. The high-\lambda economy has positive median RDD even at high K_R; the low-\lambda economy has negative median RDD at lower K_R.

Observable implication. K_R^{\text{RDD}} is endogenous to \lambda: higher ownership diffusion raises the level of robotic capital at which median RDD turns negative.

