Appendix K: Identification Details

K.1 Instrument 1 — Automation Exposure

Shift-share instrument following Acemoglu and Restrepo (2019):

\text{Exposure}_{r,t} = \sum_j \frac{L_{r,j,t_0}}{L_{r,t_0}}\cdot\Delta\text{Robots}_{j,t},

where L_{r,j,t_0}/L_{r,t_0} is the pre-period employment share of industry j in region r, and \Delta\text{Robots}_{j,t} is the change in robot installations in industry j. The IFR stock data (4.66M operational units, 542,000 installations in 2024) provide the industry-level robot data.

K.2 Instrument 2 — Ownership Diffusion

Policy discontinuities in ESOP tax treatment, privatization voucher schemes, and mandatory profit-sharing thresholds. The NCEO 2023 data (15.1M ESOP participants, $1.3T in assets) provide the coverage measure. SCF 2022 provides the participation-rate anchors (34% bottom-half income, 95% top decile).

K.3 Instrument 3 — Institutional Adaptation

Exogenous shocks to training capacity: funding discontinuities in active labor market programs, program rollouts with staggered timing. These identify A_E.

K.4 Instrument 4 — Sovereign-Equity and Public-Fund Policy Discontinuities

The 2026 policy wave: the American AI Sovereign Wealth Fund Act (one-time 50% equity transfer from major AI firms into a public fund), OpenAI's proposed 5% public equity stake, Anthropic's national-SWF proposal. These constitute exogenous shifts in \lambda_{\text{ctrl}} and \lambda_{\text{access}}, orthogonal to household-level exposure.

K.5 Instrument 5 — Cross-Regime Variation

Chen and Rithmire (2026) document 1,177 registered generative-AI services in China 2023–25, 23.2% state-linked. The Chinese diffusion-forward model and the US concentrated-private model provide \lambda-variation at similar K_R, the ideal test of the paper's central prediction.

K.6 Instrument 6 — Energy-Price Shocks

Europe's 2022 energy-price shock as an exogenous shift in p_E, testing \partial I_R/\partial p_E<0. The shock was driven by geopolitical events (Russia–Ukraine) orthogonal to European robot-adoption decisions.

