Appendix P: Cross-Regime Test Specification

P.1 Design

The central prediction is that two economies with identical K_R but different \lambda have different RDD distributions. The test compares China (diffusion-forward, state-equity \lambda) and the US (concentrated private \lambda).

P.2 Implementation

\text{RDD}_{h,t}^{\text{US}} = \alpha_0+\alpha_1 K_{R,t}+\alpha_2\lambda^{\text{US}}\theta_{h,t}\Delta V_{K,t}+\varepsilon_{h,t},

\text{RDD}_{h,t}^{\text{CN}} = \alpha_0+\alpha_1 K_{R,t}+\alpha_2\lambda^{\text{CN}}\theta_{h,t}\Delta V_{K,t}+\varepsilon_{h,t}.

The prediction is \alpha_2>0 and \lambda^{\text{CN}}>\lambda^{\text{US}} on the ownership-access dimension, so median RDD is higher in China at comparable K_R.

P.3 Data

China: Chen–Rithmire dataset (1,177 registered generative-AI services, 23.2% state-linked); UBTECH Walker S2 orders (10,000 units, 1.4B RMB). US: SCF 2022, IFR robot stock, NCEO ESOP data.

P.4 Threats

Cross-country comparison is confounded by differences in industrial structure, labor-market institutions, and data coverage. The test is informative only conditional on controlling for K_R, industry composition, and stage of development.

